N2  - CONS is a formidable adversary confronting the ELBW infant in the NICU. Invasive infections caused by CONS result in increased antibiotic exposure, prolonged hospitalization, and increased morbidity and mortality in the ELBW infant. New strategies directed at therapeutically exploitable bacterial virulence factors and host immune deficits show promise toward the prevention of infection and thus the reduction in the morbidity and mortality associated with CONS sepsis.
